From ed5f8e0adc68032afcfa6703606b57ed8ef693bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ngo Quoc Dat <datlechin@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:56:32 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] vrend: use GL_ANGLE_texture_multisample on ES 3.0 hosts

Mesa's virgl driver offers sample counts above 1 only when the host reports
texture_multisample, which vrend does with multisample textures, on OpenGL
ES from 3.1. ANGLE on Metal offers ES 3.0 and has them through
GL_ANGLE_texture_multisample, so its guests had GL_MAX_SAMPLES 1, below the
4 ES 3.0 requires.

libepoxy builds its dispatch from Khronos' gl.xml, which does not list the
extension, and aborts on the core entry points there, so they are taken
from eglGetProcAddress and stand in for glTexStorage2DMultisample,
glGetMultisamplefv and glSampleMaski in the format and sample count
checks, the texture allocation and the sample mask. The extension has no
2D multisample arrays, which such a host refuses. Shaders and the
blitter's shaders that read a multisample texture enable the extension
there. Multisample renderbuffers, core in ES 3.0, would not do:
texture_multisample also lets guests sample multisample textures, and
vrend keeps every resource a texture.

The test clears a 4-sample target and resolves it in its own format and
through the blitter's shaders into one without alpha, where the host has
multisample textures.

Signed-off-by: Ngo Quoc Dat <datlechin@gmail.com>
